    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate is headlined by **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Corbin Carroll**, who emerge as our must-start anchors with scores of 69.25 and 67.82, respectively. **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits from a massive 10% park boost against the right-handed Jos\u00e9 Soriano, and his platoon advantage serves as the primary engine for his elevated efficiency. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** remains a top-tier asset despite the negative platoon impact of facing a southpaw; his base production and the premium we place on his game-changing speed keep him in the elite tier. **Brice Turang** rounds out the top trio at 61.57, leveraging a favorable matchup against M. P\u00e9rez and a solid 9% skill boost tied to the opposing pitcher\u2019s limitations, ensuring he remains a focal point in our middle infield.\n\nThe optimization process was tightest at the corner infield and utility spots, leading to the decision to bench **Austin Riley**. Despite a respectable 45.54 score, his performance is suppressed by a difficult matchup against the elite arm of Misiorowski (2.70 xERA), which carries a 19% downward adjustment for skill. Consequently, **Kyle Karros** and **Max Muncy** retain their starts due to more favorable park factors and the necessity of managing daily efficiency caps. Managers should note that several slots remain subject to change due to pending lineups, specifically regarding **Dalton Rushing**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Alex Freeland**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Tyler Soderstrom**. Should these players shift lower in the batting order than our projections anticipate, their efficiency scores will adjust downward, potentially narrowing the gap between them and reserves like **Cole Young**. We continue to monitor the status of **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Mickey Moniak**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL.",
